  "description": "SIMULATED annual exposure layers, one 250 m raster per calendar year 2014-2019 over a 10 km window around downtown Los Angeles: the 1 km Gaussian random field plus a trend of 0.30 ug/m3 per year in the west rising to 0.50 in the east. A 3 x 3 cell nodata hole (-9999) lies 1 km east and 1 km south of the centre. The year of each layer is the calendar year of its file; the files are loaded into one table with a filename column. Not a measurement of any real exposure.",
